{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/72668-fate-destiny-and-the-sidereal-agenda","id":72668,"title":"Fate, Destiny, and the Sidereal Agenda","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T09:48:47-08:00","id":72668,"title":"Fate, Destiny, and the Sidereal Agenda","content":"The Alternate Demiurge sidebar in Shards mentions the possibility of alternate antagonists for the great conspiracy behind the Modern shard. Infernals always seemed an odd choice for that role to me given that the Sidereals are so much better at being ninjas and spinning plots, so I hit on the idea of a Modern shard in which the Maidens still attend the loom -- Samsara in this shard is a thing which dominates their agendas to the point of rendering them divine automatons, so they continue to attend the loom in person and command the Sidereals to control Creation in their name.<br /> <br /> This brings up the question of how much control over events the Sidereals could actually have in a situation where they don't have to spend every waking moment dealing with the loom or the heavenly bureaucracy, and my general unfamiliarity with the splat isn't helping me answer it terribly well. To what extent does Sidereal interference eliminate free will in those he is acting on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:08:30-08:00","id":72677,"title":"","content":"Depends on what version of weaving Destinies you use.<br /> <br /> The thing is, they don't <i>really</i> screw with free will; instead...<br /> <br /> You know how you get into a rut? Where it just seems <i>easier</i> to do something?<br /> <br /> That's what Sidereals do; increasing someone's TN to 8 when doing things they don't like, and dropping it to 6 if you are doing something they approve of. Heck, technically they can depopulate villages by making it so you have to roll for stuff like &quot;balancing while walking&quot;, if I read that chapter properly.<br /> <br /> They screw with probabilities, not free will, I guess is what I'm trying to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:33:59-08:00","id":72692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/72668-fate-destiny-and-the-sidereal-agenda#post72668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This brings up the question of how much control over events the Sidereals could actually have in a situation</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really kind of a &quot;how long is a piece of string&quot; question. Like, if you ask about particular things Sidereals can accomplish, one can point out Charms they have to do it (off the top of my head, I'll say that they have Charms to force which of several considered options you'll choose, or to go about invisibly and give you subliminal suggestions), but &quot;how much control can they have&quot; ultimately amounts to how much effort you're going to portray them putting in, and what kind of countering agents you'll present to hinder them.<br /> <br /> Like, does the setting still have the gods as banished beyond the edge of the world? Presumably not, in which case they can delegate a whole lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent does Sidereal interference eliminate free will in those he is acting on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the usual extent that somebody whose life is subject to circumstances outside of their control or subordination to others, not much.<br /> <br /> Sidereals can shape circumstances; like, if they want you to fortuitously meet somebody, they'll construct the end result and some of the lead up, and logical factors will just drive it into happening. But they can't make the future out of implausible elements, and the actual choices and motivations of people are part of that. They can't just say &quot;and then John the bus driver drove his bus into the side of a classroom, killing many children&quot;, and if they try, John's free will is probably going to generate errors in fate. When their agendas or nebulous predictions about the future find that a certain result is necessary but currently implausible, they'll work to put their own hand into changing factors to make it plausible; Sidereals can interact with John and use whatever means they have available (with their own Charms personal torments, with their sorceries and martial arts outright mind breaking or mind control) to turn John into a person who murderously hates children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:59:12-08:00","id":72708,"title":"","content":"Or, with John, they can fate him to have an accident that makes him plow into the side of a classroom. I'm sad that the rules for fate manipulation don't actually let you do that all too well, but if John was a mortal, they could toss a Descending Destiny based off Drive (what constellation is that?) that gives him a penalty to driving near schools, and then &quot;ensure&quot; that there was a patch of ice right there.<br /> <br /> They don't really get any &quot;do what I say&quot; charms, though, iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:05:10-08:00","id":72756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/72668-fate-destiny-and-the-sidereal-agenda?p=72692#post72692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, does the setting still have the gods as banished beyond the edge of the world? Presumably not, in which case they can delegate a whole lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. I do need operations in Yu-Shan to be disrupted for a while in the back story the way they are in the core Modern setting, most likely by civil war of some kind. I'm still kind of undecided on how the war with the yozis played out, but large parts of heaven don't care for what the Sidereals pulled and rebel in the aftermath. By the time of the modern day the only gods still alive in Yu-Shan are the ones that are on board with the Sidereal game plan; the rest are labeled Forbidden Gods and either forged into starmetal or escape into hiding among mortals. The Raksha are what's around the edge of Creation rather than an organized resistance movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:16:59-08:00","id":72762,"title":"","content":"All right, that probably makes a few things a fair bit harder...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:57:11-08:00","id":72782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/72668-fate-destiny-and-the-sidereal-agenda?p=72762#post72762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, that probably makes a few things a fair bit harder...</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I'm given to understand that there are millions of unemployed gods in Yu-Shan even when things are running the way they are in the core setting, so it's not like they couldn't find replacements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:03:47-08:00","id":72836,"title":"","content":"I think it might be easiest to visualize Sidereal influence on four distinct levels. The power a Sidereal Conspiracy can exert- and what that looks like- depends primarily on how much effort and presence the conspiracy can dedicate to any given place.<br /> <br /> 1 - Personal - When a Sidereal is actually stationed somewhere, their influence in that area is exceptionally strong and very difficult to root out. A Sidereal can move invisibly through the halls of power, whispering suggestions into the minds of victims and even encoding messages into somebody so that the Sidereal's social attacks could go off anywhere, at any time and come from anybody. Sidereal social magic can trample over free will pretty easily, and things like Easily-Accepted Proposition Stance mean that this control can be pretty endemic. Even if you identify who the Sidereal is, they could just be somebody- anybody- else the next day. It's also worth noting that Sidereals can kill mortals with a look and a prayer, and that death is pretty much untraceable. The solace, of course, is that powerful Sidereals who have mastered all of these powers rarely have the time to set up shop in one city and take over. Thus, we get to-<br /> <br /> 2 - Divine Control - Realistically, a powerful Sidereal who wants an area kept under control is going to assign some gods to do it. These could be familiars, spirits bound through charms, spirits bound through Terminal Sanction or just political allies. A Sidereal can force the co-operation of the spirits which govern an area, or they can bribe it with something like Willing Assumption of Chains. Speaking of that charm, a Sidereal can offer a divine agent some advantages by granting them a useful domain, which is sometimes much better than just summoning a bunch of first-circle demons to watch a place. Things to watch for: areas protected by particularly surly elementals, wars which were fought specifically so a Sidereal could bind a powerful spirit and force it into line.<br /> <br /> 3 - Physical Agents - There's nothing terribly unusual about this part. Sidereals, like any Exalt, can corral a lot of people into serving as cats-paws. A Sidereal can create or destroy an organization as they desire it, so one would probably see a lot of centered-ness to a Sidereal's pawns. If a Sidereal has left mortal friends to keep a town in line with his plans, chances are good that they all belong to a club or organization in common (although that organization doesn't have to involve the common goal at all). <br /> <br /> 4 - Destiny - This is what people focus on first, and it is both the weakest and most pervasive form of Sidereal influence. On a grand scale, it's a statistical thing- an unusually high number of people fall to this disease, or survive it. The farmers are really on the ball this year, or else there were a lot of screwups and the harvest isn't great. People suddenly start feeling a lot better after they've gone to church, and so religion becomes more popular! Stuff like that. This is all just weighting probabilities in somebody's BIG PLAN, and nor what most players care about. No, they're more interested in the champion who finds himself more likely to win at the same time that his opponent is more likely to lose. These destinies give important pawns a little more or less oomph where the Sidereal needs it, but they're not powerfully determinative in and of themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thus it is as it has always been- where a Sidereal agent can focus, they have vast control over a situation. Sidereal charms grant an incredible amount of behind-the-scenes power to a Sidereal... but they don't linger. The Sidereal has to stay there to leverage them, and the old weakness of only having 100 Sidereals rears its ugly head. A secret Sidereal hegemony rests on the points of power where individual Sidereals CAN be spared to remain and the efficacy of the agents they employ elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}